# Linked to ~/.rgignore. ripgrep reads ignore files from every parent directory, so these rules
# reach any search started below $HOME. Searches outside $HOME get them through the ripgrep config
# file that this module's init.fish generates.
#
# The `**/` prefix is required. A pattern that contains a slash is anchored to the directory holding
# this file, so a bare `.git/objects` would only ever prune $HOME/.git — never a repository found
# further down the tree.
**/.bare/logs
**/.bare/objects
**/.bare/refs
**/.git/logs
**/.git/objects
**/.git/refs
